1
00:01:41,810 --> 00:01:49,020
[Genius Girlfriend]

2
00:01:49,370 --> 00:01:51,800
[Episode 3]

3
00:01:56,310 --> 00:01:59,120
"From the abrupt to the disordered..."

4
00:02:00,340 --> 00:02:02,750
[Constantly Strive to Become Stronger;
Strive to Be Number One]

5
00:02:09,080 --> 00:02:11,240
Duan Qiyan, seriously?
You're reading philosophy?

6
00:02:11,240 --> 00:02:12,700
Do you even understand it?

7
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:15,220
Tang, can you just leave me alone?

8
00:02:16,230 --> 00:02:17,840
I'm much better than you.

9
00:02:17,770 --> 00:02:19,650
[Natural Philosophy]

10
00:02:18,030 --> 00:02:20,690
I refuse to be looked down
upon by a fool like you.

11
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:23,090
This has nothing to do with grades.

12
00:02:23,090 --> 00:02:24,910
It's mainly about one's aura.

13
00:02:25,190 --> 00:02:26,800
And with your rough aura,

14
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:28,150
you're only fit to read something like

15
00:02:27,270 --> 00:02:27,680
[Natural Philosophy]

16
00:02:28,150 --> 00:02:29,910
immortal cultivation
or martial arts novels.

17
00:02:29,910 --> 00:02:32,000
Me? Rough?

18
00:02:32,750 --> 00:02:34,780
Hey, I've finished The Little Prince.

19
00:02:34,780 --> 00:02:35,440
Here you go.

20
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:38,579
I was wrong.

21
00:02:38,910 --> 00:02:39,910
You're not rough.

22
00:02:40,150 --> 00:02:42,740
You're just too immature, little prince.

23
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:45,430
Let me tell you—

24
00:02:44,620 --> 00:02:47,980
[The Little Prince]

25
00:02:45,430 --> 00:02:46,630
the romance of The Little Prince

26
00:02:46,630 --> 00:02:48,890
is something you will never understand.

27
00:02:49,210 --> 00:02:50,210
Don't just laugh.

28
00:02:50,680 --> 00:02:52,079
What kind of book did you put
in the reading corner?

29
00:02:52,079 --> 00:02:52,940
I'd like to see.

30
00:02:53,650 --> 00:02:54,210
Guys,

31
00:02:54,210 --> 00:02:55,340
[Class Challenge Leaderboard]

32
00:02:54,360 --> 00:02:56,090
who took Tang Tingting's book?

33
00:02:57,970 --> 00:02:58,680
I have it.

34
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:01,180
Let me see.

35
00:03:02,900 --> 00:03:03,970
[Constantly Strive to Become Stronger;
Strive to Be Number One]

36
00:03:04,310 --> 00:03:07,150
The CEO's Private Sweetheart.

37
00:03:09,410 --> 00:03:10,400
Typical Tang Tingting.

38
00:03:10,250 --> 00:03:11,350
[Class Challenge Leaderboard]

39
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:11,560
This looks just like your kind of book—

40
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:14,190
shallow and a total waste of time.

41
00:03:14,470 --> 00:03:15,630
What do you know?

42
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:18,400
Web romance is also
a type of modern literature.

43
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:19,470
Don't talk nonsense
if you don't understand.

44
00:03:19,470 --> 00:03:20,840
Fine, then let me see for myself.

45
00:03:20,030 --> 00:03:21,930
[The CEO's Private Sweetheart]

46
00:03:22,360 --> 00:03:23,840
Let me read this out loud for you guys.

47
00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:26,400
Mr. Dai shouted, "Come here and sit down!"

48
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:28,310
His voice startled Shen Meng.

49
00:03:28,310 --> 00:03:30,780
Seeing that Shen Meng did not comply,
Mr. Dai pressed her step by step.

50
00:03:30,780 --> 00:03:32,000
He whispered in her ear...

51
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:32,520
Give it to me!

52
00:03:32,520 --> 00:03:33,470
"Why are you hiding?"

53
00:03:33,470 --> 00:03:34,710
"The second button of my shirt...

54
00:03:34,710 --> 00:03:37,430
-Stop reading!
-fits right into your fluttering eyelashes."

55
00:03:37,430 --> 00:03:38,160
Give it to me!

56
00:03:39,360 --> 00:03:40,590
What are you doing? Don't hit me.

57
00:03:40,590 --> 00:03:41,310
Let's talk this out.

58
00:03:41,310 --> 00:03:42,630
Don't hit me! Stop!

59
00:03:44,360 --> 00:03:45,360
What are you doing?

60
00:03:45,360 --> 00:03:46,130
Don't hit me!

61
00:03:48,250 --> 00:03:48,860
Guys,

62
00:03:49,210 --> 00:03:51,120
I finished reading
The Solitude of Prime Numbers.

63
00:03:50,280 --> 00:03:50,840
[The Solitude of Prime Numbers]

64
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:52,620
But there's no name on it.

65
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:53,440
[The Solitude of Prime Numbers]

66
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:53,660
Whose is it?

67
00:03:54,650 --> 00:03:55,150
Mine.

68
00:04:01,560 --> 00:04:04,830
[Gödel, Escher, Bach: an Eternal Golden Braid]

69
00:04:05,250 --> 00:04:06,780
How come you have this book?

70
00:04:11,180 --> 00:04:12,500
When I went to get the book,

71
00:04:12,500 --> 00:04:14,500
it was the last one left on the shelf.

72
00:04:14,930 --> 00:04:16,560
Although it is a bit challenging to read,

73
00:04:16,560 --> 00:04:18,490
I actually quite like its content.

74
00:04:18,620 --> 00:04:20,540
I guess I was meant to read it.

75
00:04:27,690 --> 00:04:29,890
[Reading Corner]

76
00:04:35,680 --> 00:04:38,010
So you didn't leave after school that day.

77
00:04:38,890 --> 00:04:39,360
What?

78
00:04:42,740 --> 00:04:43,540
It's nothing.

79
00:04:52,770 --> 00:04:54,100
I bombed the test today.

80
00:04:54,180 --> 00:04:55,870
I got a math question wrong
in the fill-in-the-blank section,

81
00:04:55,870 --> 00:04:57,270
and only scored 118.

82
00:04:58,190 --> 00:04:59,520
But my parents said that

83
00:04:59,690 --> 00:05:02,060
not getting a perfect score
means it's a total failure,

84
00:05:02,060 --> 00:05:03,590
they even called me a loser.

85
00:05:04,180 --> 00:05:05,640
But I really tried my best.

86
00:05:05,860 --> 00:05:07,920
I'm so tired. I really want to escape.

87
00:05:08,370 --> 00:05:09,680
But where can I go?

88
00:05:19,980 --> 00:05:20,640
Jin Baihui.

89
00:05:23,980 --> 00:05:25,390
I finished reading your book.

90
00:05:25,390 --> 00:05:26,120
It was great.

91
00:05:27,100 --> 00:05:30,010
I noticed some annotations inside—
I assume they're yours.

92
00:05:30,010 --> 00:05:31,070
I really like them.

93
00:05:36,330 --> 00:05:37,980
In 1915, Emmy Noether

94
00:05:37,980 --> 00:05:39,300
developed Noether's theorem.

95
00:05:39,300 --> 00:05:40,560
She has a famous quote:

96
00:05:41,120 --> 00:05:42,320
"Mathematics is free

97
00:05:43,159 --> 00:05:45,420
and unrestrained by the outside world."

98
00:05:46,659 --> 00:05:48,590
What exactly are you trying to say?

99
00:05:50,370 --> 00:05:51,180
I mean,

100
00:05:51,770 --> 00:05:54,130
the essence of learning is exploration.

101
00:05:54,510 --> 00:05:55,840
And exploration is fun.

102
00:05:56,010 --> 00:05:57,060
I hope you can discover

103
00:05:57,060 --> 00:05:58,060
the joy in it.

104
00:05:59,740 --> 00:06:01,940
Don't put so much pressure on yourself.

105
00:06:05,040 --> 00:06:05,660
[The Kite Runner]

106
00:06:07,770 --> 00:06:09,500
You're just talking nonsense.

107
00:06:21,300 --> 00:06:23,100
Did you come here just to pity me?

108
00:06:24,120 --> 00:06:24,510
I didn't.

109
00:06:24,510 --> 00:06:26,040
Who needs your pity anyway?

110
00:06:26,500 --> 00:06:27,430
What do you know?

111
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:28,930
Do you really think a few comforting words

112
00:06:28,930 --> 00:06:30,190
can solve my problems?

113
00:06:30,810 --> 00:06:32,010
Stop acting so smart.

114
00:06:43,270 --> 00:06:44,000
Lin Zhixia.

115
00:06:45,330 --> 00:06:46,260
Don't be so smug.

116
00:06:46,860 --> 00:06:48,990
I will surpass you. I definitely will!

117
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:10,610
Are you still upset about
what happened with Jin Baihui?

118
00:07:11,040 --> 00:07:12,720
I'm reflecting on my experiences

119
00:07:12,720 --> 00:07:14,380
and trying to learn from them.

120
00:07:14,620 --> 00:07:16,720
I think I really need to work on my EQ.

121
00:07:18,040 --> 00:07:18,770
Jiang Yubai,

122
00:07:18,860 --> 00:07:20,240
let me know directly

123
00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:21,270
if you find any issues with me,

124
00:07:21,270 --> 00:07:22,530
and I'll correct them.

125
00:07:26,040 --> 00:07:27,130
There's no need for that.

126
00:07:27,130 --> 00:07:27,740
Why?

127
00:07:28,130 --> 00:07:29,590
Just keep being yourself.

128
00:07:29,980 --> 00:07:31,600
Once people get to know you better,

129
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:32,920
they'll all grow to like you.

130
00:07:32,920 --> 00:07:33,720
Liar.

131
00:07:34,240 --> 00:07:37,000
Since I was a kid, you're the only one
who has ever felt that way.

132
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:38,420
I really want to fix this.

133
00:07:39,060 --> 00:07:40,860
Just tell me what the problem is.

134
00:07:41,600 --> 00:07:43,159
Is it because I'm too blunt?

135
00:07:47,750 --> 00:07:48,610
So it really is!

136
00:07:50,159 --> 00:07:52,450
Your expression says I'm too blunt.

137
00:07:53,800 --> 00:07:54,450
No.

138
00:07:59,170 --> 00:08:01,310
Don't tell me I've said something

139
00:08:01,310 --> 00:08:03,710
that accidentally hurt your feelings too?

140
00:08:07,270 --> 00:08:08,310
When I was seven,

141
00:08:08,310 --> 00:08:09,970
my mom took me to get an IQ test.

142
00:08:10,240 --> 00:08:12,370
It was a free test
at the City Central Hospital.

143
00:08:12,370 --> 00:08:14,480
My IQ was 174 back then.

144
00:08:14,920 --> 00:08:17,520
The doctor said
the number would keep going up.

145
00:08:17,870 --> 00:08:20,070
Jiang Yubai, what's your IQ?

146
00:08:20,160 --> 00:08:21,490
Are you smarter than me?

147
00:08:24,310 --> 00:08:25,010
No.

148
00:08:25,570 --> 00:08:27,030
I wasn't that petty, was I?

149
00:08:31,630 --> 00:08:34,480
Your expression clearly says
I did hurt your feelings.

150
00:08:34,480 --> 00:08:35,100
Maybe,

151
00:08:36,220 --> 00:08:37,460
occasionally.

152
00:08:38,130 --> 00:08:40,390
But I actually don't remember much of it.

153
00:08:40,510 --> 00:08:42,200
We are such good friends now.

154
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:43,669
Just say what's on your mind.

155
00:08:43,669 --> 00:08:44,820
Don't make me guess.

156
00:08:55,150 --> 00:08:55,880
For example,

157
00:08:56,910 --> 00:08:58,920
the first semester of fourth grade...

158
00:08:58,920 --> 00:09:01,650
You still remember something
from that long ago?

159
00:09:04,720 --> 00:09:05,850
I remember you said,

160
00:09:05,910 --> 00:09:09,150
"Only Jiang Yubai would listen
to me talk about physics and math,

161
00:09:09,150 --> 00:09:11,550
even though he didn't understand a thing."

162
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:15,270
I guess I really was out of line.

163
00:09:15,270 --> 00:09:18,070
And then there's your
"Human Observation Diary."

164
00:09:18,210 --> 00:09:18,680
[Human Observation Diary
is a preliminary review of research]

165
00:09:18,700 --> 00:09:19,130
[On the thinking patterns
of ordinary people.]

166
00:09:19,160 --> 00:09:19,770
[By observing the author's deskmate,
Jiang Yubai,]

167
00:09:19,630 --> 00:09:20,770
You want to study me

168
00:09:19,790 --> 00:09:20,240
[And his cognitive limitations,
this paper further explores

169
00:09:20,270 --> 00:09:20,820
[The thinking patterns of ordinary people]

170
00:09:21,250 --> 00:09:22,120
just because

171
00:09:22,500 --> 00:09:23,800
I'm an ordinary human?

172
00:09:24,010 --> 00:09:24,480
Yeah.

173
00:09:27,980 --> 00:09:29,310
And you even wrote in it,

174
00:09:29,670 --> 00:09:30,840
"I found out that Jiang Yubai

175
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:33,840
knows nothing about
the famous General Relativity."

176
00:09:34,320 --> 00:09:36,100
I thought you said you barely remembered?

177
00:09:36,100 --> 00:09:38,840
How come you're reciting all this
like it was yesterday?

178
00:09:38,840 --> 00:09:41,040
Fine, I'll keep that in mind from now on.

179
00:09:41,340 --> 00:09:43,050
I feel like half of my competitive streak

180
00:09:43,050 --> 00:09:44,890
was shaped by you.

181
00:09:46,880 --> 00:09:48,410
I will admit my mistakes and correct them.

182
00:09:48,410 --> 00:09:49,750
I'm apologizing to you right now.

183
00:09:49,750 --> 00:09:51,410
Jiang Yubai is not an ordinary human—

184
00:09:51,410 --> 00:09:53,870
he's a great genius.

185
00:09:55,580 --> 00:09:56,100
No need.

186
00:09:56,750 --> 00:09:58,330
I'll prove it with my own ability.

187
00:09:58,330 --> 00:09:59,790
Okay, genius Jiang Yubai.

188
00:10:02,350 --> 00:10:04,150
I shouldn't have told you this
in the first place.

189
00:10:04,150 --> 00:10:04,680
Let's go.

190
00:10:04,860 --> 00:10:06,120
Yes, King Jiang Yubai.

191
00:10:06,600 --> 00:10:07,200
Let's go.

192
00:10:19,700 --> 00:10:22,460
I'll just take another
two minutes of your recess.

193
00:10:22,460 --> 00:10:23,250
At the end of this month,

194
00:10:23,250 --> 00:10:26,130
the province-wide
Rising Star Math Competition

195
00:10:26,650 --> 00:10:28,100
will be held in the city.

196
00:10:28,720 --> 00:10:29,580
This competition

197
00:10:29,580 --> 00:10:31,270
is a three-member team event.

198
00:10:31,740 --> 00:10:32,980
So if you are interested,

199
00:10:32,980 --> 00:10:34,820
you can form your own teams to sign up.

200
00:10:34,820 --> 00:10:37,370
Please hand in your registration forms
to me before next Friday.

201
00:10:37,370 --> 00:10:37,790
Okay?

202
00:10:38,860 --> 00:10:39,240
Here.

203
00:10:40,360 --> 00:10:41,160
Pass these on.

204
00:10:41,750 --> 00:10:42,750
Class dismissed.

205
00:11:01,480 --> 00:11:02,210
Jiang Yubai,

206
00:11:03,030 --> 00:11:04,340
about that math competition just now,

207
00:11:04,340 --> 00:11:05,940
do you want to team up with me?

208
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:07,530
Are you participating too?

209
00:11:07,770 --> 00:11:09,010
Then the three of us can team up.

210
00:11:09,010 --> 00:11:10,270
That makes a full team!

211
00:11:13,130 --> 00:11:13,860
Jiang Yubai,

212
00:11:14,820 --> 00:11:17,220
I was asking if you wanted
to team up with me.

213
00:11:25,370 --> 00:11:27,580
The Three Departments
and Six Ministries system

214
00:11:27,580 --> 00:11:28,580
was the core of
the central bureaucratic system

215
00:11:28,580 --> 00:11:30,910
from the Sui and Tang
to the Song and the Yuan.

216
00:11:30,910 --> 00:11:33,860
It marked the maturity of
the ancient Chinese bureaucratic system.

217
00:11:33,860 --> 00:11:35,390
It divided
the central administrative organs

218
00:11:35,390 --> 00:11:39,210
into three major systems:
decision-making, review, and execution.

219
00:11:39,210 --> 00:11:41,070
Teaming up with Jiang Yubai means

220
00:11:41,150 --> 00:11:43,350
the math competition is a piece of cake.

221
00:11:44,100 --> 00:11:46,960
We're already
a sufficient condition for victory.

222
00:11:48,530 --> 00:11:49,620
But before the competition,

223
00:11:49,620 --> 00:11:52,980
I need to help him go over
the probability problems one more time.

224
00:11:52,980 --> 00:11:55,180
He always gets stuck on Bayes' theorem.

225
00:12:09,340 --> 00:12:11,500
I've made a pre-competition schedule.

226
00:12:11,500 --> 00:12:12,700
If we follow this plan,

227
00:12:12,700 --> 00:12:14,630
we can definitely get first place.

228
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:20,670
Lin Zhixia.

229
00:12:22,340 --> 00:12:23,670
I can't team up with you.

230
00:12:33,510 --> 00:12:34,240
Jiang Yubai.

231
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:37,260
Come here for a second.

232
00:12:41,400 --> 00:12:42,740
Why won't you team up with me

233
00:12:42,740 --> 00:12:44,000
for this competition?

234
00:12:45,170 --> 00:12:45,840
Lin Zhixia.

235
00:12:47,170 --> 00:12:48,580
As long as we team up,

236
00:12:48,720 --> 00:12:50,600
there will be no suspense
in this competition.

237
00:12:50,600 --> 00:12:52,360
Or rather, as long as you're in it,

238
00:12:52,360 --> 00:12:54,250
there won't be much suspense
in this competition.

239
00:12:54,250 --> 00:12:56,650
Because you've always been in first place.

240
00:12:57,580 --> 00:12:58,320
To be honest,

241
00:12:59,270 --> 00:13:01,740
you really are the most
capable person I've ever met.

242
00:13:01,740 --> 00:13:03,700
Wouldn't it be nice
to win first place with me?

243
00:13:03,700 --> 00:13:04,620
That would be nice.

244
00:13:04,620 --> 00:13:06,720
It's just that
I don't want to rely on you to win.

245
00:13:06,720 --> 00:13:09,580
More than that, I don't want to
just be the genius's teammate.

246
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:11,720
I also want to see how big
the gap between us really is

247
00:13:11,720 --> 00:13:13,720
when we compete against each other.

248
00:13:21,480 --> 00:13:22,340
All right then.

249
00:13:22,890 --> 00:13:24,290
I accept your challenge.

250
00:13:25,670 --> 00:13:26,600
Let's make a bet.

251
00:13:27,650 --> 00:13:28,170
A bet?

252
00:13:31,620 --> 00:13:32,600
Let's make a bet.

253
00:13:33,170 --> 00:13:35,770
Jiang Yubai,
if you get first place in our grade,

254
00:13:35,770 --> 00:13:37,370
then I'll call you Mr. Jiang.

255
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:39,100
But if I get first place,

256
00:13:39,170 --> 00:13:41,620
then you should call me
Ms. Lin to show your respect.

257
00:13:41,620 --> 00:13:42,480
How about that?

258
00:13:45,860 --> 00:13:47,270
Ms. Lin.

259
00:13:48,250 --> 00:13:49,980
What? What did you just call me?

260
00:13:52,370 --> 00:13:54,200
Ms. Lin.

261
00:13:57,410 --> 00:13:59,410
You want me to call you Ms. Lin again?

262
00:14:00,500 --> 00:14:02,500
So you still remember, Jiang Yubai.

263
00:14:02,750 --> 00:14:03,950
Of course I remember.

264
00:14:04,790 --> 00:14:06,390
That's my childhood trauma.

265
00:14:06,580 --> 00:14:07,780
Then I'm sorry to say,

266
00:14:07,860 --> 00:14:10,520
you're going
to have "childhood trauma" again.

267
00:14:10,980 --> 00:14:11,740
If you lose,

268
00:14:12,010 --> 00:14:14,390
you have to buy me
strawberry milk for a month

269
00:14:14,390 --> 00:14:16,720
as compensation for my emotional distress.

270
00:14:16,720 --> 00:14:17,700
I lose,

271
00:14:18,010 --> 00:14:19,940
and I still have to compensate you?

272
00:14:20,550 --> 00:14:21,240
Of course.

273
00:14:22,050 --> 00:14:22,910
Because of you,

274
00:14:23,530 --> 00:14:25,220
I missed out on the chance

275
00:14:25,220 --> 00:14:27,650
of participating in a competition
with a good friend.

276
00:14:27,650 --> 00:14:29,740
Don't you think you owe me that much?

277
00:14:31,260 --> 00:14:32,390
But what if I win?

278
00:14:33,100 --> 00:14:33,700
You win?

279
00:14:41,240 --> 00:14:43,300
I never thought about that scenario.

280
00:15:02,290 --> 00:15:03,890
Just say what you want to say.

281
00:15:11,860 --> 00:15:12,940
Do you know about

282
00:15:13,460 --> 00:15:16,260
the province-wide
Rising Star Math Competition?

283
00:15:17,120 --> 00:15:17,620
I know.

284
00:15:17,960 --> 00:15:18,960
I signed up for it.

285
00:15:19,700 --> 00:15:21,300
I need to pick two teammates.

286
00:15:21,870 --> 00:15:22,890
They don't have to be from my class—

287
00:15:22,890 --> 00:15:24,870
sophomores or seniors are all fine.

288
00:15:24,870 --> 00:15:26,930
Can you join the competition with me?

289
00:15:27,620 --> 00:15:29,250
My older brother is my student.

290
00:15:29,250 --> 00:15:32,050
My older brother is my student!

291
00:15:33,050 --> 00:15:33,980
Call me Teacher.

292
00:15:34,170 --> 00:15:36,230
-Call her Teacher.
-Call me Teacher.

293
00:15:36,370 --> 00:15:38,430
-Call her Teacher.
-Call me Teacher.

294
00:15:39,980 --> 00:15:40,840
Sorry, I can't.

295
00:15:44,390 --> 00:15:45,790
Zeqiu.

296
00:15:46,510 --> 00:15:48,200
I'm sincerely inviting you.

297
00:15:48,740 --> 00:15:50,010
Can you...

298
00:15:50,320 --> 00:15:51,050
No, I can't.

299
00:15:57,080 --> 00:15:59,210
You look ridiculous when you act cute.

300
00:16:01,720 --> 00:16:03,580
I'm full. Figure it out yourself.

301
00:16:11,970 --> 00:16:14,500
I'm really optimistic
about this Paul George card.

302
00:16:14,500 --> 00:16:17,560
This card's value
is definitely going up in the future.

303
00:16:17,670 --> 00:16:18,630
How about mine?

304
00:16:18,790 --> 00:16:19,620
Cousins.

305
00:16:20,050 --> 00:16:22,870
I went through a lot of trouble
to get it from my older brother.

306
00:16:22,870 --> 00:16:23,820
If you ask me,

307
00:16:24,360 --> 00:16:26,420
both of your cards are just mediocre.

308
00:16:27,270 --> 00:16:29,150
I'm currently looking into

309
00:16:29,150 --> 00:16:31,410
a limited-edition Kobe Gold Refractor.

310
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:34,000
Limited edition?

311
00:16:34,670 --> 00:16:36,030
What are you dreaming about?

312
00:16:36,030 --> 00:16:38,200
That's not something
us regular high school kids can have.

313
00:16:38,200 --> 00:16:39,660
Don't be so quick to judge.

314
00:16:39,870 --> 00:16:41,330
To be honest with you guys,

315
00:16:41,630 --> 00:16:44,030
I'm about to get one.

316
00:16:45,390 --> 00:16:46,120
Give it to me!

317
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:48,460
How are you going to get it?

318
00:16:48,630 --> 00:16:50,530
Don't ask, just wait and see.

319
00:16:50,980 --> 00:16:51,720
Let me see.

320
00:16:52,480 --> 00:16:53,150
Let me see.

321
00:16:53,150 --> 00:16:54,050
Be careful.

322
00:16:54,050 --> 00:16:54,580
I'm fine.

323
00:16:57,270 --> 00:16:58,000
Wan Chunlei.

324
00:16:58,320 --> 00:17:00,650
I've signed up for
the Rising Star Math Competition.

325
00:17:00,650 --> 00:17:02,440
Would you like to team up with me?

326
00:17:02,440 --> 00:17:05,440
No, thanks.
I've already teamed up with someone else.

327
00:17:08,640 --> 00:17:09,569
Hey, hear me out.

328
00:17:10,440 --> 00:17:11,960
Because...

329
00:17:11,960 --> 00:17:14,589
Duan Qiyan,
do you have a competition partner yet?

330
00:17:14,589 --> 00:17:16,190
Do you want to team up with me?

331
00:17:16,920 --> 00:17:18,440
Me? I think I'll pass.

332
00:17:18,440 --> 00:17:20,040
I've been quite busy lately.

333
00:17:20,640 --> 00:17:22,440
But your grades are really good, right?

334
00:17:22,440 --> 00:17:24,440
It would be such a pity if you skip it.

335
00:17:24,680 --> 00:17:26,440
Well, my grades are good for sure,

336
00:17:26,440 --> 00:17:28,109
but my ambitions lie elsewhere.

337
00:17:28,109 --> 00:17:28,640
Besides,

338
00:17:29,160 --> 00:17:30,680
I might not be in last place,

339
00:17:30,680 --> 00:17:32,000
but I'm definitely not
in first place either.

340
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:32,750
So I'll pass.

341
00:17:33,160 --> 00:17:35,270
With me as your teammate, we'll be fine.

342
00:17:35,270 --> 00:17:37,160
Lin Zhixia, can't you take a hint?

343
00:17:37,640 --> 00:17:39,000
He has already rejected you several times.

344
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:40,160
He doesn't want to team up with you.

345
00:17:40,160 --> 00:17:40,960
It's not like everyone

346
00:17:40,960 --> 00:17:42,160
has to participate in that competition.

347
00:17:42,160 --> 00:17:43,440
We're on our lunch break,

348
00:17:43,440 --> 00:17:46,370
and you just keep going on and on.
You're so annoying!

349
00:18:04,010 --> 00:18:04,640
Tang.

350
00:18:06,160 --> 00:18:07,640
Don't you think you're

351
00:18:07,640 --> 00:18:09,240
targeting her a bit too much?

352
00:18:09,460 --> 00:18:11,810
The three of us were way louder
than Lin Zhixia just now.

353
00:18:11,810 --> 00:18:13,000
Why are you only shouting at her?

354
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:13,590
Shut up!

355
00:18:13,960 --> 00:18:15,160
You're annoying too.

356
00:18:35,140 --> 00:18:35,800
Lin Zhixia.

357
00:18:38,640 --> 00:18:39,370
Shen Fuxuan?

358
00:18:40,330 --> 00:18:41,830
I came specifically to find you.

359
00:18:41,830 --> 00:18:42,590
Find me?

360
00:18:44,700 --> 00:18:47,500
That book of yours in the reading corner
at the start of the semester,

361
00:18:47,500 --> 00:18:48,500
Gödel...

362
00:18:48,500 --> 00:18:49,850
Gödel, Escher, Bach:

363
00:18:49,850 --> 00:18:51,250
An Eternal Golden Braid.

364
00:18:51,750 --> 00:18:52,150
Right.

365
00:18:53,510 --> 00:18:55,310
That book is really hard to read.

366
00:18:55,310 --> 00:18:56,200
I hope one day

367
00:18:56,790 --> 00:18:59,030
I can fully digest it
and discuss it with you.

368
00:18:59,030 --> 00:18:59,630
Of course.

369
00:19:01,900 --> 00:19:03,500
About the math competition,

370
00:19:03,610 --> 00:19:05,470
have you found any teammates yet?

371
00:19:06,440 --> 00:19:07,140
Not yet.

372
00:19:08,500 --> 00:19:09,050
Then,

373
00:19:10,790 --> 00:19:11,850
can you count me in?

374
00:19:12,660 --> 00:19:13,860
Are you willing to...

375
00:19:16,030 --> 00:19:17,030
You're saying...

376
00:19:18,460 --> 00:19:19,070
Of course!

377
00:19:19,500 --> 00:19:21,760
But why are you willing
to team up with me?

378
00:19:23,030 --> 00:19:24,590
Participating in the competition with you

379
00:19:24,590 --> 00:19:26,250
should be quite interesting.

380
00:19:29,250 --> 00:19:32,180
Actually, I've known about you
for quite a long time.

381
00:19:32,380 --> 00:19:33,840
My mom mentioned you to me.

382
00:19:34,980 --> 00:19:36,290
Your mom is...

383
00:19:36,940 --> 00:19:37,740
Shen Zhaohua.

384
00:19:38,900 --> 00:19:40,430
Professor Shen is your mom?

385
00:19:40,810 --> 00:19:42,290
We've stayed in touch.

386
00:19:42,500 --> 00:19:44,300
She often asks about my studies.

387
00:19:45,460 --> 00:19:47,550
It's probably because
it's rare for her to meet someone

388
00:19:47,550 --> 00:19:48,900
as talented as you.

389
00:19:50,220 --> 00:19:53,080
I'm just interested
in the ocean and the starry sky,

390
00:19:53,140 --> 00:19:54,940
and I read some books about them.

391
00:19:55,500 --> 00:19:57,460
I bet you've had plenty of opportunities

392
00:19:57,460 --> 00:19:59,420
to be exposed to interesting things
since you were little.

393
00:19:59,420 --> 00:20:00,110
I...

394
00:20:00,810 --> 00:20:02,010
I guess it's alright.

395
00:20:03,750 --> 00:20:04,680
Then it's a deal.

396
00:20:05,270 --> 00:20:06,600
We'll team up together.

397
00:20:08,500 --> 00:20:09,500
Get one more teammate,

398
00:20:09,500 --> 00:20:11,110
and our team will be complete.

399
00:20:11,110 --> 00:20:12,710
I'll go find other students.

400
00:20:17,880 --> 00:20:18,610
Kid,

401
00:20:19,570 --> 00:20:20,400
regarding how to solve

402
00:20:20,400 --> 00:20:22,510
the local micro-turbulence
in the aquarium,

403
00:20:22,510 --> 00:20:23,790
do you have any ideas?

404
00:20:24,330 --> 00:20:26,330
I think we can install
artificial coral reefs.

405
00:20:26,330 --> 00:20:28,610
When micro-turbulence passes
through the reefs,

406
00:20:28,610 --> 00:20:30,610
it breaks down into milder water currents,

407
00:20:30,610 --> 00:20:32,470
reducing its destructive force.

408
00:20:53,200 --> 00:20:53,800
Excuse me,

409
00:20:55,530 --> 00:20:58,330
do you want to participate
in the math competition?

410
00:20:58,330 --> 00:20:59,060
No, we don't.

411
00:20:59,110 --> 00:21:00,440
We are not capable of that.

412
00:21:00,440 --> 00:21:01,570
Sorry to bother you.

413
00:21:07,240 --> 00:21:07,840
Excuse me,

414
00:21:08,380 --> 00:21:10,920
does either of you want
to participate in the math competition?

415
00:21:10,920 --> 00:21:12,050
No, we don't.

416
00:21:35,480 --> 00:21:37,480
Jiang Yubai, we are preparing
for the competition.

417
00:21:37,480 --> 00:21:39,210
Can you stop being distracted?

418
00:21:40,440 --> 00:21:42,240
If Lin Zhixia can't find teammates,

419
00:21:42,240 --> 00:21:43,750
she might not be able
to participate at all.

420
00:21:43,750 --> 00:21:44,810
Isn't that better?

421
00:21:45,070 --> 00:21:47,800
We have a better chance
of winning if she doesn't.

422
00:21:49,070 --> 00:21:51,600
Winning would be meaningless
if she doesn't.

423
00:21:54,570 --> 00:21:55,330
I mean,

424
00:21:56,510 --> 00:21:58,310
if Lin Zhixia doesn't participate,

425
00:21:58,310 --> 00:21:59,240
even if we win,

426
00:21:59,240 --> 00:22:01,440
other students will think we win unfairly.

427
00:22:01,440 --> 00:22:02,850
What's the point of a competition

428
00:22:02,850 --> 00:22:04,650
if the highest score is removed?

429
00:22:04,700 --> 00:22:06,230
This is a team competition.

430
00:22:06,380 --> 00:22:07,980
If she can't even form a team,

431
00:22:08,660 --> 00:22:09,860
she has already lost.

432
00:22:25,920 --> 00:22:32,880
[Death Scythe]

433
00:22:28,070 --> 00:22:29,600
Do you really like Han Geng?

434
00:22:29,810 --> 00:22:31,640
It's rare for boys to like him.

435
00:22:32,910 --> 00:22:35,630
[Of course, I have every album of his.]

436
00:22:35,700 --> 00:22:40,740
[Hey, I don't know
what kind of person you are yet.]

437
00:22:35,850 --> 00:22:38,220
I don't know
what kind of person you are yet.

438
00:22:38,220 --> 00:22:39,880
Are you handsome in real life?

439
00:22:40,760 --> 00:22:43,030
[Are you handsome in real life?]

440
00:22:43,030 --> 00:22:47,060
[Well, not bad. A little handsome.]

441
00:22:47,080 --> 00:22:50,880
[They all say I look like Han Geng.]

442
00:22:50,610 --> 00:22:52,640
Really? Do you have any photos?

443
00:22:55,070 --> 00:23:01,370
[I don't take photos. I'm introverted.]

444
00:23:01,290 --> 00:23:03,790
It doesn't matter.
We've been chatting for so long.

445
00:23:01,410 --> 00:23:03,710
[Well, it doesn't matter.
We've been chatting for so long.]

446
00:23:03,730 --> 00:23:05,860
[And we're both his fans.]

447
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:05,680
And we're both his fans.

448
00:23:05,810 --> 00:23:08,050
Do you want to meet offline
and make friends?

449
00:23:05,880 --> 00:23:12,100
[Do you want to meet offline
and make friends?]

450
00:23:12,210 --> 00:23:16,090
[Sure.]

451
00:23:31,590 --> 00:23:33,550
Duan Qiyan, why are you here?

452
00:23:36,140 --> 00:23:37,400
I'm going to the beach.

453
00:23:39,790 --> 00:23:41,120
What are you doing here?

454
00:23:43,500 --> 00:23:44,760
None of your business.

455
00:23:46,720 --> 00:23:48,050
You dressed up today.

456
00:23:48,720 --> 00:23:49,780
Look at this dress.

457
00:23:50,720 --> 00:23:51,750
Are you on a date?

458
00:23:52,460 --> 00:23:53,200
Yes.

459
00:23:53,200 --> 00:23:54,900
I am on a date.

460
00:23:55,110 --> 00:23:55,960
The friend I am meeting later

461
00:23:55,960 --> 00:23:57,070
is very handsome.

462
00:23:57,070 --> 00:23:58,330
He looks like Han Geng.

463
00:23:59,420 --> 00:24:01,280
Just go. Don't get in the way here.

464
00:24:03,160 --> 00:24:04,660
Looks like Han Geng?

465
00:24:06,510 --> 00:24:07,640
Then do you think...

466
00:24:08,830 --> 00:24:10,110
I look like Han Geng?

467
00:24:13,070 --> 00:24:14,250
Angel's Tears.

468
00:24:20,500 --> 00:24:21,680
Duan Qiyan, I...

469
00:24:23,480 --> 00:24:25,160
Angel's Tears.

470
00:24:25,880 --> 00:24:26,830
What were you thinking?

471
00:24:26,830 --> 00:24:28,830
Giving yourself such a cheesy name?

472
00:24:29,640 --> 00:24:31,480
What does my name have to do with you?

473
00:24:31,480 --> 00:24:33,110
You added me out of nowhere

474
00:24:33,110 --> 00:24:34,240
and didn't even tell me.

475
00:24:34,240 --> 00:24:36,270
It's none of your business if I add you.

476
00:24:36,270 --> 00:24:37,110
Besides,

477
00:24:37,380 --> 00:24:38,510
you accepted it, didn't you?

478
00:24:38,510 --> 00:24:38,940
I...

479
00:24:42,180 --> 00:24:43,570
Wait, stop it.

480
00:24:43,880 --> 00:24:45,160
You have to think about it this way.

481
00:24:45,160 --> 00:24:46,480
At least, I was the one who added you.

482
00:24:46,480 --> 00:24:49,110
Think about it.
At the prime of your youth,

483
00:24:49,110 --> 00:24:51,570
a young girl like you
meets someone offline.

484
00:24:51,750 --> 00:24:53,200
What if you run into a bad guy?

485
00:24:53,200 --> 00:24:54,240
Meeting a liar like you

486
00:24:54,240 --> 00:24:57,720
-is worse than meeting a bad guy.
-Tang Tingting, let go!

487
00:24:57,920 --> 00:24:58,720
No, I won't.

488
00:24:58,720 --> 00:25:00,160
If you don't, I'll fight back.

489
00:25:00,160 --> 00:25:01,590
Don't you dare!

490
00:25:01,750 --> 00:25:03,030
Three, two, one.

491
00:25:03,180 --> 00:25:05,290
You... let go, Tang Tingting.

492
00:25:05,290 --> 00:25:06,440
You let go!

493
00:25:07,920 --> 00:25:10,000
Tingting, are you two playing around?

494
00:25:10,000 --> 00:25:10,730
Yeah, we are.

495
00:25:11,000 --> 00:25:12,000
Take care, Auntie Liu.

496
00:25:12,000 --> 00:25:13,240
Alright, have fun.

497
00:25:13,240 --> 00:25:13,840
Take care.

498
00:25:17,200 --> 00:25:18,440
Are you letting go or not?

499
00:25:18,440 --> 00:25:19,240
You let go.

500
00:25:19,420 --> 00:25:20,270
You... you...

501
00:25:20,270 --> 00:25:21,200
let go.

502
00:25:21,200 --> 00:25:22,110
You let go.

503
00:25:23,030 --> 00:25:24,940
Tang Tingting, let go.

504
00:25:25,200 --> 00:25:26,600
I won't. You let go first.

505
00:25:26,790 --> 00:25:27,660
If you don't,

506
00:25:28,050 --> 00:25:28,960
I'm going to suffocate.

507
00:25:28,960 --> 00:25:29,490
Hurry up.

508
00:25:29,640 --> 00:25:30,810
You let go first.

509
00:25:31,400 --> 00:25:32,270
Be gentle.

510
00:25:33,160 --> 00:25:33,820
Duan Qiyan.

511
00:25:35,200 --> 00:25:36,060
Tang Tingting!

512
00:25:36,830 --> 00:25:38,070
Uncle, he hit me!

513
00:25:38,550 --> 00:25:38,960
Dad,

514
00:25:39,510 --> 00:25:40,240
I didn't.

515
00:25:41,110 --> 00:25:41,570
Auntie,

516
00:25:42,070 --> 00:25:43,050
she started it.

517
00:25:46,070 --> 00:25:46,940
What happened?

518
00:25:47,790 --> 00:25:49,920
Tell me what happened.

519
00:25:50,680 --> 00:25:53,010
I just got back
and saw you bullying a girl.

520
00:25:54,920 --> 00:25:56,380
How do I usually teach you?

521
00:25:56,550 --> 00:25:57,880
As a gentleman,

522
00:25:58,070 --> 00:25:59,110
you must first...

523
00:25:59,330 --> 00:26:00,310
Be responsible.

524
00:26:00,310 --> 00:26:00,770
Then...

525
00:26:00,920 --> 00:26:01,590
Know how to listen,

526
00:26:01,590 --> 00:26:03,310
and not interrupt others casually.

527
00:26:03,310 --> 00:26:03,750
And?

528
00:26:03,960 --> 00:26:04,820
Respect women.

529
00:26:05,090 --> 00:26:05,640
Did you do that?

530
00:26:05,640 --> 00:26:06,090
No.

531
00:26:08,400 --> 00:26:10,550
Tingting's mom, I'm really sorry.

532
00:26:10,550 --> 00:26:11,590
I've failed to teach my son well.

533
00:26:11,590 --> 00:26:12,790
Sorry for the trouble.

534
00:26:12,790 --> 00:26:14,920
-Sorry. Sorry.
-Don't say that, Duan.

535
00:26:15,400 --> 00:26:17,500
We both know our own kids best.

536
00:26:17,740 --> 00:26:19,050
It takes two to tango.

537
00:26:19,440 --> 00:26:20,140
Yes.

538
00:26:21,590 --> 00:26:22,350
Don't hit the kid.

539
00:26:22,350 --> 00:26:24,070
You even tackled him!

540
00:26:24,070 --> 00:26:26,750
A girl tackled a boy?

541
00:26:26,880 --> 00:26:28,140
Is that how a lady acts?

542
00:26:28,270 --> 00:26:29,110
Exactly.

543
00:26:29,110 --> 00:26:29,640
Unbelievable.

544
00:26:29,640 --> 00:26:31,850
Auntie, you need to be the judge.

545
00:26:32,200 --> 00:26:33,070
Today, I was online

546
00:26:33,070 --> 00:26:34,800
and played a little joke on her.

547
00:26:34,850 --> 00:26:35,920
And she tackled me.

548
00:26:35,920 --> 00:26:36,750
Was that necessary?

549
00:26:36,750 --> 00:26:37,740
It really wasn't.

550
00:26:37,740 --> 00:26:38,200
Enough.

551
00:26:38,790 --> 00:26:40,450
You think you're in the right?

552
00:26:41,590 --> 00:26:42,590
Online?

553
00:26:44,310 --> 00:26:45,960
Weren't you doing homework at home today?

554
00:26:45,960 --> 00:26:47,660
When were you online?

555
00:26:48,350 --> 00:26:49,700
Um, Tingting's mom.

556
00:26:50,770 --> 00:26:52,830
If there's nothing else, we'll head back.

557
00:26:52,830 --> 00:26:54,590
Alright, sorry for the trouble.

558
00:26:54,590 --> 00:26:56,050
Please don't be so polite.

559
00:26:56,070 --> 00:26:57,330
-I won't see you off.
-Bye. Bye.

560
00:26:57,330 --> 00:26:58,140
Bye. Bye.

561
00:27:01,460 --> 00:27:01,980
I...

562
00:27:02,160 --> 00:27:03,960
I'll throw the trash out for you.

563
00:27:05,110 --> 00:27:05,920
So gentlemanly.

564
00:27:05,920 --> 00:27:07,000
See you. See you.

565
00:27:07,000 --> 00:27:07,920
Thanks, Duan.

566
00:27:10,830 --> 00:27:13,430
I'll settle the score with you
when we get home.

567
00:27:13,770 --> 00:27:14,900
Here, throw it away.

568
00:27:26,520 --> 00:27:28,860
[Points Card]

569
00:27:37,590 --> 00:27:38,000
Dad.

570
00:27:38,830 --> 00:27:39,760
Have some water.

571
00:27:41,590 --> 00:27:42,500
Thanks.

572
00:27:43,010 --> 00:27:44,420
My pleasure, Dad.

573
00:27:46,940 --> 00:27:47,400
Tell me.

574
00:27:48,610 --> 00:27:51,140
How many points
have you saved up on this card?

575
00:27:55,900 --> 00:27:56,610
Not many.

576
00:27:58,660 --> 00:27:59,290
It's fine.

577
00:27:59,500 --> 00:28:01,590
I can check it even if you don't tell me.

578
00:28:01,590 --> 00:28:03,050
I used to play too, right?

579
00:28:03,240 --> 00:28:04,170
I've been there.

580
00:28:04,900 --> 00:28:06,660
But the rule in our family

581
00:28:06,900 --> 00:28:10,010
is leniency for confession
and severity for resistance.

582
00:28:10,010 --> 00:28:11,030
You know this.

583
00:28:11,250 --> 00:28:12,500
So I suggest

584
00:28:12,830 --> 00:28:14,310
you just tell me.

585
00:28:14,940 --> 00:28:16,340
I promise I won't hit you.

586
00:28:18,770 --> 00:28:19,510
Really?

587
00:28:20,440 --> 00:28:21,750
Of course.

588
00:28:22,010 --> 00:28:22,740
Just tell me.

589
00:28:26,720 --> 00:28:28,480
Fifty or sixty thousand.

590
00:28:30,480 --> 00:28:31,880
Fifty or sixty thousand?

591
00:28:38,180 --> 00:28:40,160
Dad, I'll never go again!

592
00:28:40,420 --> 00:28:41,420
I mean it!

593
00:28:41,680 --> 00:28:42,240
Dad!

594
00:28:43,010 --> 00:28:43,460
Dad!

595
00:28:44,570 --> 00:28:46,170
Duan Wenming, be civilized!

596
00:28:46,270 --> 00:28:47,460
It's illegal to beat kids!

597
00:28:47,460 --> 00:28:48,000
Ouch!

598
00:28:48,220 --> 00:28:49,460
Ouch, it hurts!

599
00:28:53,180 --> 00:28:53,980
Class is over.

600
00:28:54,000 --> 00:28:55,640
Let's go downstairs and play basketball.

601
00:28:55,640 --> 00:28:56,170
Let's go.

602
00:28:57,050 --> 00:28:58,570
I'm covered in bruises.

603
00:28:59,500 --> 00:29:00,880
I think I'll skip it.

604
00:29:07,010 --> 00:29:09,180
It's all because of that Tang Tingting.

605
00:29:09,180 --> 00:29:11,310
She ruined my sports player card plan.

606
00:29:12,090 --> 00:29:14,570
The limited-edition Kobe card
you mentioned last time?

607
00:29:14,570 --> 00:29:15,270
Yes.

608
00:29:15,810 --> 00:29:16,570
I bet

609
00:29:16,570 --> 00:29:18,000
I found the only one in the whole city,

610
00:29:18,000 --> 00:29:19,400
right at Lele Toys"R"Us.

611
00:29:19,810 --> 00:29:21,720
That's their grand prize.

612
00:29:21,940 --> 00:29:24,000
It takes 100,000 points to redeem it.

613
00:29:24,250 --> 00:29:25,700
I worked hard to save up for over a week.

614
00:29:25,700 --> 00:29:26,900
I finally managed...

615
00:29:27,140 --> 00:29:28,850
to save half of the points, but...

616
00:29:28,850 --> 00:29:29,660
my dad

617
00:29:29,660 --> 00:29:31,460
snapped the points card in half.

618
00:29:39,810 --> 00:29:42,000
Aren't you short of a teammate right now?

619
00:29:42,000 --> 00:29:43,240
Duan Qiyan is now completely

620
00:29:43,240 --> 00:29:44,370
obsessed with this.

621
00:29:44,810 --> 00:29:46,380
You can start from this point

622
00:29:46,380 --> 00:29:47,640
and get him on the team.

623
00:29:51,250 --> 00:29:53,480
Arcade sports player card.

624
00:29:54,460 --> 00:29:55,680
That's my blind spot.

625
00:29:57,240 --> 00:29:59,500
I haven't really dealt with this before.

626
00:29:59,610 --> 00:30:01,700
But we have a short holiday coming up.

627
00:30:02,380 --> 00:30:03,580
Let's go check it out.

628
00:30:05,830 --> 00:30:08,290
I've never even seen
these machines before.

629
00:30:09,140 --> 00:30:10,250
Duan Qiyan tried for so long

630
00:30:10,250 --> 00:30:11,420
and couldn't win the grand prize.

631
00:30:11,420 --> 00:30:12,350
Can we do it?

632
00:30:13,250 --> 00:30:14,310
Let's give it a try.

633
00:30:14,460 --> 00:30:16,260
Duan Qiyan is just too obsessed.

634
00:30:16,550 --> 00:30:18,050
I think there are some tricks

635
00:30:18,050 --> 00:30:20,420
and patterns to these games.

636
00:30:23,590 --> 00:30:25,190
Sir, your tickets are saved.

637
00:30:27,250 --> 00:30:28,180
Okay, thank you.

638
00:30:33,140 --> 00:30:34,670
What are you two doing here?

639
00:30:35,110 --> 00:30:35,770
Duan Qiyan,

640
00:30:36,290 --> 00:30:37,620
how about we make a deal?

641
00:30:38,420 --> 00:30:39,020
What deal?

642
00:30:40,290 --> 00:30:42,480
If we help you redeem
the sports player card,

643
00:30:42,480 --> 00:30:44,720
you'll join Lin Zhixia's
math competition group.

644
00:30:44,720 --> 00:30:45,580
What do you say?

645
00:30:46,220 --> 00:30:47,680
Are you kidding me, Jiang?

646
00:30:48,250 --> 00:30:50,180
The sports player card
has been there for so long.

647
00:30:50,180 --> 00:30:52,240
Do you think you can easily redeem it?

648
00:30:57,250 --> 00:30:59,480
Anyway, we are confident.

649
00:31:00,010 --> 00:31:02,140
It just depends on whether you want it.

650
00:31:03,740 --> 00:31:04,220
Fine.

651
00:31:04,740 --> 00:31:06,770
If you can really
get me the card,

652
00:31:07,090 --> 00:31:08,490
forget about teaming up,

653
00:31:08,770 --> 00:31:10,300
I can even be your follower.

654
00:31:13,610 --> 00:31:14,980
These are my remaining tokens.

655
00:31:14,980 --> 00:31:16,050
You guys take them and play.

656
00:31:16,050 --> 00:31:17,570
Everything here is a scam.

657
00:31:17,640 --> 00:31:18,830
I've quit now.

658
00:31:19,460 --> 00:31:20,720
Bye-bye. I'm leaving.

659
00:31:26,420 --> 00:31:28,790
[Commemorative Kobe Card]

660
00:31:29,680 --> 00:31:31,810
Why do I suddenly feel so competitive?

661
00:31:32,610 --> 00:31:33,140
Me too.

662
00:31:33,850 --> 00:31:35,840
[Commemorative Kobe Card]

663
00:31:38,330 --> 00:31:40,590
Although it's my first time at an arcade,

664
00:31:40,850 --> 00:31:43,140
it's even more fun than I imagined.

665
00:31:44,570 --> 00:31:46,170
The music rising and falling

666
00:31:46,610 --> 00:31:47,940
and the colorful lights

667
00:31:48,400 --> 00:31:49,700
seemed to turn the whole world

668
00:31:49,700 --> 00:31:52,010
into a giant candy box.

669
00:32:02,530 --> 00:32:05,010
We tried all the games.

670
00:32:06,220 --> 00:32:08,250
The sense of accomplishment
from completing challenges together

671
00:32:08,250 --> 00:32:10,720
is more real and thrilling than any prize.

672
00:32:11,400 --> 00:32:13,680
We even forgot
our original intention while playing,

673
00:32:13,680 --> 00:32:16,160
which was to help Duan Qiyan
get the sports player card

674
00:32:16,160 --> 00:32:18,890
to make him my teammate
for the math competition.

675
00:32:25,700 --> 00:32:28,230
When the doll
we wanted most finally dropped,

676
00:32:29,240 --> 00:32:30,370
I suddenly realized

677
00:32:31,110 --> 00:32:33,700
my very first time at an arcade

678
00:32:34,110 --> 00:32:35,920
was with Jiang Yubai.

679
00:32:37,030 --> 00:32:39,160
It feels like whatever we do together,

680
00:32:39,400 --> 00:32:41,460
we're blessed with incredible luck.

681
00:32:42,530 --> 00:32:43,070
Perhaps,

682
00:32:44,050 --> 00:32:46,010
having a good friend by your side

683
00:32:47,160 --> 00:32:48,680
is the greatest reward

684
00:32:49,940 --> 00:32:50,940
bestowed by fate.

685
00:32:58,920 --> 00:33:00,720
Congratulations to both of you.

686
00:33:10,270 --> 00:33:10,670
How...

687
00:33:11,570 --> 00:33:12,170
did you...

688
00:33:12,880 --> 00:33:14,070
do that?

689
00:33:14,160 --> 00:33:15,250
Never mind that.

690
00:33:15,550 --> 00:33:17,110
According to our previous agreement,

691
00:33:17,110 --> 00:33:18,940
can you join my team now?

692
00:33:22,310 --> 00:33:24,840
Are you really going
to join the competition?

693
00:33:27,630 --> 00:33:28,960
Look, Lin Zhixia,

694
00:33:29,310 --> 00:33:30,270
I don't really

695
00:33:30,660 --> 00:33:33,160
like doing stressful things.

696
00:33:33,770 --> 00:33:36,230
So let's just forget
about the competition.

697
00:33:36,480 --> 00:33:37,830
Didn't we agree on this?

698
00:33:38,480 --> 00:33:39,750
Don't you want the card?

699
00:33:39,750 --> 00:33:41,250
Yes, I do want it.

700
00:33:41,680 --> 00:33:42,140
But

701
00:33:43,030 --> 00:33:45,550
let me think about the competition
a bit more.

702
00:33:45,550 --> 00:33:47,500
Why are you breaking your promise?

703
00:33:48,000 --> 00:33:50,000
I'm not breaking my promise, Jiang.

704
00:33:51,880 --> 00:33:53,200
Zhixia is here.

705
00:33:53,200 --> 00:33:55,200
-Hello, Mr. Duan.
-Long time no see.

706
00:33:56,110 --> 00:33:57,550
This is my classmate, Jiang Yubai.

707
00:33:57,550 --> 00:33:58,220
Hello, Mr. Duan.

708
00:33:58,220 --> 00:33:58,880
Hello.

709
00:33:59,270 --> 00:33:59,940
Have a seat.

710
00:33:59,940 --> 00:34:01,340
Make yourselves at home.

711
00:34:02,310 --> 00:34:04,240
You haven't visited in a long time.

712
00:34:04,310 --> 00:34:05,440
What do you want for dinner?

713
00:34:05,440 --> 00:34:06,370
I'll arrange it.

714
00:34:06,830 --> 00:34:08,150
We don't need to stay for dinner.

715
00:34:08,150 --> 00:34:09,280
I came to find Duan Qiyan

716
00:34:09,280 --> 00:34:11,280
to talk about the math competition.

717
00:34:11,510 --> 00:34:12,570
Math competition?

718
00:34:14,280 --> 00:34:15,610
What math competition?

719
00:34:15,840 --> 00:34:16,770
You didn't know?

720
00:34:17,820 --> 00:34:18,780
I really didn't.

721
00:34:20,760 --> 00:34:21,760
It's like this, Mr. Duan.

722
00:34:21,760 --> 00:34:23,380
This is a very important

723
00:34:23,380 --> 00:34:24,980
provincial math competition.

724
00:34:24,980 --> 00:34:27,090
The best students
in the province are participating.

725
00:34:27,090 --> 00:34:28,949
Because it's a team competition,

726
00:34:28,980 --> 00:34:31,310
most of our classmates have formed teams.

727
00:34:31,500 --> 00:34:33,440
But Duan Qiyan hasn't signed up yet.

728
00:34:33,440 --> 00:34:35,960
So we wanted to try to convince him.

729
00:34:36,320 --> 00:34:37,150
Just give it a try,

730
00:34:37,150 --> 00:34:38,750
even if the chances are slim.

731
00:34:40,630 --> 00:34:41,440
So you mean

732
00:34:41,440 --> 00:34:42,960
this kid didn't even want

733
00:34:42,960 --> 00:34:44,230
to participate in the math competition.

734
00:34:44,230 --> 00:34:45,429
Is that what you mean?

735
00:34:46,110 --> 00:34:47,110
No, Dad.

736
00:34:47,400 --> 00:34:49,050
I've been planning it.

737
00:34:49,510 --> 00:34:50,510
I just

738
00:34:50,510 --> 00:34:52,380
don't know which team to join.

739
00:34:53,230 --> 00:34:55,820
I take this competition very seriously.

740
00:34:56,070 --> 00:34:57,600
I was planning to win a prize

741
00:34:57,630 --> 00:34:58,890
to give you a surprise.

742
00:35:00,510 --> 00:35:01,640
Isn't that perfect?

743
00:35:01,840 --> 00:35:03,610
Lin Zhixia is the best in the school.

744
00:35:03,610 --> 00:35:05,470
Isn't this the best opportunity?

745
00:35:05,760 --> 00:35:06,560
That's right.

746
00:35:07,260 --> 00:35:08,920
If you can team up with Zhixia,

747
00:35:09,360 --> 00:35:10,690
isn't that a good thing?

748
00:35:10,730 --> 00:35:12,390
What were you thinking about?

749
00:35:14,670 --> 00:35:15,460
Sure.

750
00:35:16,010 --> 00:35:16,870
Then I'll join.

751
00:35:17,320 --> 00:35:19,850
We'll start making plans
when school starts.

752
00:35:20,150 --> 00:35:23,420
Secure second
and aim for first in this competition.

753
00:35:25,510 --> 00:35:26,800
Quite ambitious.

754
00:35:26,800 --> 00:35:28,400
Secure second and aim for first.

755
00:35:28,400 --> 00:35:28,730
Fine.

756
00:35:29,360 --> 00:35:31,510
Anyway, I always

757
00:35:31,510 --> 00:35:33,570
give clear rewards and punishments,

758
00:35:33,760 --> 00:35:35,800
and I always keep my word.

759
00:35:37,190 --> 00:35:38,590
Please help him out more.

760
00:35:39,230 --> 00:35:41,130
Don't just chat. Have some fruit.

761
00:35:41,320 --> 00:35:42,580
You guys keep talking.

762
00:35:42,710 --> 00:35:45,710
I'm counting on you
to secure second and aim for first.

763
00:35:55,230 --> 00:35:55,820
Great.

764
00:35:56,190 --> 00:35:57,840
With Shen Fuxuan and Duan Qiyan,

765
00:35:57,840 --> 00:35:59,700
my competition team is complete.

766
00:36:20,080 --> 00:36:27,750
♪ Wandering light wind
drifts past your pupils ♪

767
00:36:28,860 --> 00:36:33,090
♪ One second of encounter,
heartstrings stirred ♪

768
00:36:33,710 --> 00:36:37,180
♪ The story feels altogether different ♪

769
00:36:39,280 --> 00:36:47,020
♪ How to describe
my whimsical wandering dream? ♪

770
00:36:39,280 --> 00:36:39,900
What are you doing?

771
00:36:48,270 --> 00:36:52,490
♪ You softly answer my quirky side ♪

772
00:36:52,840 --> 00:36:53,960
There was a leaf on your head.

773
00:36:52,880 --> 00:36:56,220
♪ Such bliss to finally be understood ♪

774
00:36:57,690 --> 00:37:00,930
♪ The moon drifts past the window ♪

775
00:36:57,760 --> 00:36:58,760
What else can I do?

776
00:37:02,450 --> 00:37:06,030
♪ How am I to understand? ♪

777
00:37:03,130 --> 00:37:03,880
I mean,

778
00:37:05,150 --> 00:37:06,900
how did a leaf get on my head?

779
00:37:07,450 --> 00:37:08,490
♪ About you ♪

780
00:37:08,050 --> 00:37:09,530
Why did it fall on my head?

781
00:37:09,880 --> 00:37:14,220
♪ The moment our eyes met,
my world came alive with color ♪

782
00:37:14,890 --> 00:37:19,260
♪ Could this be how love begins? ♪

783
00:37:19,780 --> 00:37:22,760
♪ These unspoken feelings
are so hard to figure out ♪

784
00:37:20,360 --> 00:37:21,320
There's a formula relating wind speed V,

785
00:37:21,320 --> 00:37:22,710
the falling leaf's initial height H,

786
00:37:22,710 --> 00:37:24,820
and wind direction θ.

787
00:37:23,340 --> 00:37:28,740
♪ Hidden deep within your gaze ♪

788
00:37:29,060 --> 00:37:33,490
♪ Sometimes, I imagine
drifting beyond the skies with you ♪

789
00:37:30,780 --> 00:37:32,320
If even a falling leaf's trajectory

790
00:37:32,320 --> 00:37:34,110
can be predicted by a formula,

791
00:37:34,040 --> 00:37:38,060
♪ Shimmering light
dances over the flower in bloom ♪

792
00:37:35,420 --> 00:37:37,220
then encounters between people

793
00:37:37,500 --> 00:37:38,760
might also be a gentle algorithm

794
00:37:38,760 --> 00:37:40,550
quietly run by the universe.

795
00:37:38,880 --> 00:37:41,950
♪ After all we've been through,
our fates remain intertwined ♪

796
00:37:42,030 --> 00:37:43,570
This is both scientific certainty

797
00:37:42,630 --> 00:37:49,120
♪ Perhaps fate favors me now ♪

798
00:37:44,480 --> 00:37:46,090
and emotional coincidence.

799
00:37:47,440 --> 00:37:49,100
But eventually, all formulas

800
00:37:49,840 --> 00:37:51,980
will collapse into one true equation.

801
00:38:07,340 --> 00:38:11,680
♪ The moment our eyes met,
my world came alive with color ♪

802
00:38:12,350 --> 00:38:16,720
♪ Could this be how love begins? ♪

803
00:38:17,240 --> 00:38:20,220
♪ These unspoken feelings
are so hard to figure out ♪

804
00:38:20,800 --> 00:38:26,250
♪ Hidden deep within your gaze ♪

805
00:38:26,530 --> 00:38:30,960
♪ The moment our eyes met,
my world was filled with hope ♪

806
00:38:31,540 --> 00:38:35,900
♪ Dim tender touches turn out to be love ♪

807
00:38:36,420 --> 00:38:39,250
♪ Unsettling thoughts at last unfold ♪

808
00:38:39,990 --> 00:38:45,270
♪ I return the moment you glance back ♪

809
00:38:45,720 --> 00:38:49,800
♪ If reunion is fated ♪

810
00:38:50,690 --> 00:38:54,100
♪ Wish upon that dust speck
amid flowing light ♪
